###############################################################################
# "Library" OData V4 test model - vocabulary annotations
#
# Start the server first:  dotnet run --project src/LibraryService
# Every request carries the result actually observed against .NET 10.0 with
# Microsoft.AspNetCore.OData 9.5.0. Read-only except for the cascade section,
# which deletes - run this file top to bottom and restart for a clean slate.
#
# Annotations live in $metadata, so most of this file is one request - the one
# below - and the shapes it has to contain. What it *does* exercise as requests
# is the second half: every capability term the container states is claimed
# because the request under it behaves that way, and every constraint term is
# claimed because the seeded data satisfies it. A term nobody checked does not
# belong in the metadata.
#
# The annotations of the reference model itself are listed in service.http;
# everything here is this server's own addition, and a deliberate deviation
# from the reference EDMX - see ../FEATURE-COVERAGE.md.
###############################################################################

@host = http://localhost:5091/odata/v4/library
@book = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@audiobook = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@ebook = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@collectorsItem = 77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777

###############################################################################
# The document
###############################################################################

### 200 - 69 annotations over 24 terms of 4 vocabularies. Every one of the value
### shapes CSDL knows for a constant appears, and each is the shape the term's
### declared type calls for - which is what the emitter is for:
###
###   Bool         Core.Computed, Core.Immutable, Core.AdditionalProperties
###   String       Core.Description, Measures.Unit, Validation.Pattern
###   Int          Validation.MaxItems, Measures.Scale, Validation.Minimum (Edm.Byte)
###   Float        Validation.Minimum/Maximum on Medium/PopularityScore (Edm.Double)
###   EnumMember   Core.Permissions
###   Collection   Core.AcceptableMediaTypes, Capabilities.SupportedFormats
###   PropertyPath Core.OptimisticConcurrency
###   Record       Core.AlternateKeys, Capabilities.SearchRestrictions
###
### Note the two Validation.Minimum shapes: the term is typed Edm.PrimitiveType,
### so the *value* decides - Int="1" on Book/PageCount, Float="0" on
### Medium/PopularityScore. Targets covered: entity type, complex type property,
### enum type, enum member, entity set, singleton, container, function, action
### and operation parameter.
GET {{host}}/$metadata

###############################################################################
# Capability terms on the container - each one is what the request shows
###############################################################################

### 200 - Capabilities.BatchSupported="true"
### (the payload variants are in batch.http; this only shows $batch answers)
POST {{host}}/$batch
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requests": [ { "id": "1", "method": "get", "url": "Media?$top=1" } ] }

### 200 - Capabilities.KeyAsSegmentSupported="true". The key as its own segment
### resolves to the same entity as the parenthesised form.
GET {{host}}/Members/1

### 200 - the parenthesised form, for comparison: identical body
GET {{host}}/Members(1)

### 200 - Capabilities.QuerySegmentSupported="true". Query options in the body
### of a POST, which is what the term is about.
POST {{host}}/Media/$query
Content-Type: text/plain

$top=1&$select=Title

### 200 - Capabilities.AsynchronousRequestsSupported="false". The preference is
### *ignored*, not honoured: the answer is the ordinary 200 with no
### Preference-Applied header and no 202/Location. Stating false is therefore
### the truthful annotation.
GET {{host}}/Media?$top=1
Prefer: respond-async

### 404 - Capabilities.CrossJoinSupported="false". $crossjoin is not routed at
### all, so the term says so rather than leaving the client to find out.
GET {{host}}/$crossjoin(Media,Copies)

### 200 - Capabilities.SupportedFormats="application/json": the only format the
### service answers in, and the one every response above carries.
GET {{host}}/Media?$top=1&$format=application/json

###############################################################################
# What is derived from the EF Core model rather than written
#
# Four facts are stated once, in LibraryContext, and translated into the EDM:
#   .IsConcurrencyToken()  -> Core.OptimisticConcurrency, and @odata.etag
#   HasPrecision(p, s)     -> the Precision / Scale facets
#   DeleteBehavior.Cascade -> <OnDelete Action="Cascade"/>
#   HasComment(...)        -> Core.Description
# Copy/Condition is deliberately *not* [ConcurrencyCheck]: that attribute is
# read by both stacks, so it would prove nothing. See ../IMPLEMENTATION.md.
###############################################################################

### 200 - every copy carries @odata.etag, computed from Condition. The EDM knows
### Condition is the token only because it was translated out of the EF model.
GET {{host}}/Copies

### 200 - Core.Description="Shelf mark within the branch." on Copy/Location_
### comes from the EF column comment, which is also COMMENT ON COLUMN
### "Copies"."Location_" in db/01-schema.sql. One statement, two outputs.
GET {{host}}/Copies?$select=Location_

### 200 - Precision="9" Scale="2" on Member/Balance and Precision="5" Scale="2"
### on Loan/LateFee are EF's HasPrecision, not a second declaration in
### EdmModelBuilder. The facet and the numeric column cannot disagree.
GET {{host}}/Members?$select=Balance

###############################################################################
# Core.AcceptableMediaTypes - the declared type is the type actually served
###############################################################################

### 200 - Content-Type: application/epub+zip, as EBook declares
GET {{host}}/Media({{ebook}})/$value

### 200 - Content-Type: audio/mpeg, as Audiobook/Sample declares
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})/Library.Catalog.Audiobook/Sample

### 200 - Content-Type: audio/mpeg, as AudiobookChapter declares
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})/Library.Catalog.Audiobook/Chapters(1)/$value

###############################################################################
# Constraint terms - the seeded data satisfies every one of them
#
# None of the *validation* terms is enforced: they describe the model to a
# client reading $metadata, and the runtime does not read them. That is the ⚠️
# in FEATURE-COVERAGE.md. What these requests show is that the claims are true
# of the data.
#
# The managed-property terms are the exception - Core.Computed, Core.Immutable
# and Core.Permissions *are* enforced, in the section below.
###############################################################################

### 200 - Validation.Pattern="^[0-9]{13}$" on PrintMedium/ISBN: 9783518188002,
### 13 digits. Also Validation.Minimum=0 / Maximum=18 on Book/AgeRating (16)
### and Validation.Minimum=1 on Book/PageCount (320).
GET {{host}}/Media/Library.Catalog.Book?$select=ISBN,AgeRating,PageCount

### 200 - the second ISBN in the seed, 9770000000001, likewise 13 digits. It
### sits on the Magazine, which has no collection cast of its own, so the
### alternate key is the way to it.
GET {{host}}/Media/Library.Catalog.PrintMedium(ISBN='9770000000001')

### 200 - Validation.Minimum=0 / Maximum=10 on Medium/PopularityScore:
### 3.0, 4.5, 5.2, 7.4, 8.0, 9.1, 9.9
GET {{host}}/Media?$orderby=PopularityScore&$select=PopularityScore

### 200 - Validation.Minimum=0 / Maximum=5 on Copy/Condition: 1, 2, 3.
### Measures.Unit="kg" with Measures.Scale=2 on Copy/WeightKg: 0.42, 0.41, 0.09.
GET {{host}}/Copies?$select=Condition,WeightKg

### 200 - Validation.MaxItems=20 on Medium/Keywords: 3 at most in the seed
GET {{host}}/Media?$select=Keywords

### 200 - Measures.DurationGranularity="minutes" on AudioMedium/Duration:
### PT1H52M, a whole number of minutes with no seconds component
GET {{host}}/Media/Library.Catalog.Audiobook?$select=Duration

### 200 - the other AudioMedium, the DVD: PT2H33M, likewise whole minutes
GET {{host}}/Media(66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666)

### 200 - Measures.ISOCurrency="EUR" on Member/Balance: 12.50 and 0.00.
### Core.Permissions=Read on the same property *is* enforced - see below.
GET {{host}}/Members?$select=Balance

### 200 - Core.AdditionalProperties on CollectorsItem: the type is open, and
### Appraisal and Insured are the undeclared properties it carries
GET {{host}}/Media({{collectorsItem}})

###############################################################################
# Managed properties are enforced
#
# The spec leaves no room here (Protocol 11.4.3): "Key and other properties
# marked as read-only in metadata (including computed properties) [...] can be
# omitted from the request. If the request contains a value for one of these
# properties, the service MUST ignore that value when applying the update."
#
# So the value is dropped, not rejected - a 400 would be a deviation of its own.
# Which is exactly why a generated client leaves such a property out of the
# payload: nothing in the response tells a caller the value went nowhere.
#
# See ../IMPLEMENTATION.md - one global filter for the delta-shaped writes, and
# a helper for POST/PUT, which bind the whole entity and have nothing to narrow.
###############################################################################

### 204 - Core.Immutable on Loan/LoanedAt: the PATCH carries a new LoanedAt and
### a new DueDate. Only DueDate is applied.
PATCH {{host}}/Loans(88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888)
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "LoanedAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "DueDate": "2026-12-01"
}

### 200 - LoanedAt is still 2026-06-01T10:00:00Z, DueDate is 2026-12-01
GET {{host}}/Loans(88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888)

### 201 - Core.Computed on Medium/PopularityScore: sent as 99, stored as null.
### The server generates this one on insert and update alike, so there is no
### operation in which a client value counts.
POST {{host}}/Media
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "@odata.type": "#Library.Catalog.Book",
  "Title": "Computed Probe",
  "Language": "de",
  "PageCount": 10,
  "AgeRating": 0,
  "ISBN": "9780000009901",
  "PopularityScore": 99
}

### 201 - Core.Permissions=Read on Member/Balance: sent as 999, stored as 0.
### Read-only is read-only on insert too, not only on update.
POST {{host}}/Members
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Name": "Permissions Probe",
  "PreviousAddresses": [],
  "Balance": 999
}

### 204 - PUT replaces the entity, and the properties a client may not write
### keep their stored value rather than being reset. The spec exempts exactly
### these from the reset an omission otherwise causes.
PUT {{host}}/Members(2)
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Name": "Bob Beispiel Renamed",
  "PreviousAddresses": [],
  "Balance": 777
}

### 200 - Name took, Balance is still 0.00
GET {{host}}/Members(2)?$select=Name,Balance

###############################################################################
# Capabilities: the four <OnDelete Action="Cascade"/> match what the database
# does. Each pair below is: what is there, then what is left after the delete.
#
# Last in the file, because these are the only requests here that change the
# store - everything above reads. Restart for a clean slate.
###############################################################################

### 200 - one loan and one reservation belong to member 1
GET {{host}}/Loans?$select=Id

### 204 - Member/Loans and Member/Reservations both cascade
DELETE {{host}}/Members(1)

### 200 - empty: the loan went with the member
GET {{host}}/Loans?$select=Id

### 200 - the DVD has one copy
GET {{host}}/Copies?$filter=MediumId eq 66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666

### 204 - Medium/Copies cascades
DELETE {{host}}/Media(66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666)

### 200 - empty: the copy went with the medium
GET {{host}}/Copies?$filter=MediumId eq 66666666-6666-6666-6666-666666666666

### 200 - the audiobook has two contained chapters
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})/Library.Catalog.Audiobook/Chapters

### 204 - Audiobook/Chapters cascades
DELETE {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})

### 200 - and an empty collection, not a 404. The chapters really are gone with
### their audiobook; what answers 200 is the contained path never asking
### whether its parent exists, which is this implementation's doing and not the
### cascade's - see limitations.http. The parent itself answers 404.
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})/Library.Catalog.Audiobook/Chapters

### 404 - the audiobook
GET {{host}}/Media({{audiobook}})
